(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Descriptors (PY5c; CPython's Objects/descrobject.c, funcobject.c's classmethod and staticmethod,"] [9 1 "// classobject.c's method, typeobject.c's super and slot wrappers): bound methods, functions as"] [10 1 "// descriptors, classmethod, staticmethod, property, __slots__' members, super, the slot wrappers"] [11 1 "// that show a built-in type's slots as methods, and the attributes of types, functions and methods."] [15 2 "// MethodWrapperType is method-wrapper (descrobject.c's _PyMethodWrapper_Type, queue 290): a slot wrapper bound to an"] [16 2 "// instance ((2).__pow__, object().__str__), a *Method whose Func is a *slotWrapper; inspect's _NonUserDefinedCallables"] [17 2 "// tell it from a Python bound method"] [19 2 "// ClassMethodDescrType is classmethod_descriptor (descrobject.c's PyClassMethodDescr_Type, queue 290): a built-in"] [20 2 "// type's class method as its class holds it (dict.__dict__['fromkeys']), a *ClassMethod not made by classmethod()"] [21 2 "// around a *Builtin"] [32 1 "// Method is a bound method: a function and the object it is bound to."] [44 1 "// ClassMethod and StaticMethod wrap a callable."] [46 12 "// made by classmethod(...), not a built-in type's"] [58 1 "// isDescr: c is a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor (a *Builtin not wrapped by classmethod())."] [74 1 "// directBase is b among s's bases (its Base when it has no Bases)."] [87 1 "// Property is property(fget, fset, fdel, doc)."] [90 28 "// nil when unset (prop_name NULL, queue 304: __name__ = None is a name)"] [91 28 "// a subclass of property"] [92 2 "// getterDoc is the doc taken from the getter (getter_doc); dict and slots a subclass's instance's (queue 304:"] [93 2 "// property_init's subclass rule puts __doc__ there)"] [106 1 "// Member is a __slots__ entry's descriptor."] [115 1 "// Super is super(type, obj)."] [124 1 "// slotWrapper is a built-in type's slot as a method (wrapper_descriptor)."] [133 1 "// mappingProxy is a type's __dict__ read only."] [136 11 "// the type whose __dict__ it is, or nil"] [137 11 "// the mapping, when it is no dict (mappingproxy(UserDict()))"] [140 1 "// proxied is the mapping behind p: a built-in type's __dict__ is its dict with the getsets and the own slots' wrappers"] [141 1 "// its subscript finds (ownSlot), as one dict (builtinTypeDict; queue 313, review 307's finding 3: keys, items, len and"] [142 1 "// iteration missed int's real and every slot wrapper, which in, [] and .get found)"] [153 1 "// slotdefOrder: the slots' names in typeobject.c's slotdefs order (add_operators fills a static type's dict so),"] [154 1 "// __new__ first (its tp_new wrapper goes in before them)"] [166 1 "// builtinTypeDicts: each built-in type's merged __dict__, kept while its dict and the types' epoch stand"] [175 1 "// builtinTypeDict is t's __dict__ as CPython's type_ready_fill_dict fills it: the own slots' wrappers (add_operators),"] [176 1 "// then the dict's entries (pyi's methods, in their order), then the getsets and members (type_add_members,"] [177 1 "// type_add_getset) in their declaration order, then __doc__ (type_dict_set_doc); a name the dict has is the dict's"] [221 28 "// type_dict_set_doc, last"] [243 1 "// newWrappers are the built-in types' __new__ objects, one each."] [251 1 "// slotWrappers keep one wrapper per type and name, so that int.__repr__ is int.__repr__ (enum compares"] [252 1 "// a class's methods with its data type's and object's; PY5e, part 2b)."] [255 1 "// slotWrapperFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [263 3 "// METH_COEXIST (queue 290): the method its type defines beside the slot, a method_descriptor"] [264 3 "// (frozenset.__contains__ bound is a builtin_function_or_method: keyword.iskeyword)"] [265 3 "// objectDescr: bound to the instance itself, as the slot wrapper was (a dict subclass's __missing__:"] [266 3 "// urllib.parse's _Quoter(dict).__getitem__)"] [275 1 "// coexistMethods are the built-in types' METH_COEXIST methods (dict_methods', list_methods', set_methods' and"] [276 1 "// frozenset_methods' __getitem__ and __contains__): method descriptors where the other slots have slot wrappers."] [296 5 "// object's own slots take the instance itself, not a built-in subclass's value: object.__str__ of an"] [297 5 "// int subclass is repr(self), its class's __repr__ (queue 287: test_enum's __str__ = object.__str__)"] [303 2 "// the number protocol's binary methods (__add__, __radd__, __iadd__ ...): the Binary, RBinary and InPlace"] [304 2 "// slots, NotImplemented when they do not apply (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200: test_asyncio reads int.__add__)"] [329 6 "// wrap_ternaryfunc_r: the operands swapped, the modulus third"] [342 22 "// wrap_indexargfunc"] [353 4 "// object_str: tp_repr, never the type's own __str__ (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: a class with"] [354 4 "// __str__ = object.__str__, doctest's DocTestCase, recursed without end)"] [475 5 "// dict_subscript sees self's type: a subclass's d.__getitem__(k) calls its __missing__ as d[k] does"] [476 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [477 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [585 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [586 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [590 3 "// tp_new_wrapper's builtin: object.__new__'s __self__ is object, its __qualname__ object.__new__ (queue 290:"] [591 3 "// inspect drops its $type parameter)"] [640 6 "// unicode__format__, long__format__, float___format__, complex___format__: an empty spec is the"] [641 6 "// subclass's str() (queue 287: int's gave the int's text, test_enum's overridden __str__)"] [646 19 "// object.__format__ is str(self), the instance's own __str__ (queue 287)"] [680 1 "// hackCheck is hackcheck: m's __setattr__ called on self, whose built-in base nearest to its type overrides it"] [681 1 "// (object.__setattr__(str, ...) would jump over type's own)."] [691 22 "// of the built-in bases one can reach here, only type overrides tp_setattro"] [698 1 "// objectDir is object.__dir__: the instance's dictionary's keys and its class's attributes."] [717 2 "// object___dir___impl: no class merged when __class__ is missing (queue 328: test_builtin's test_dir, a"] [718 2 "// __class__ slot never set)"] [750 3 "// object's wrappers are made on demand (slotWrapperFor), add_operators' names here"] [773 1 "// superArgs are super()'s zero arguments: the running function's first argument and its __class__ cell."] [811 2 "// supercheck: a proxy's __class__ (a class it pretends to be an instance of)"] [838 2 "// method_reduce (classobject.c): getattr(self, the function's name)"] [853 2 "// functions as descriptors, bound methods"] [860 2 "// types.MethodType(func, instance) (method_new)"] [886 2 "// method_descr_get: a bound method is not bound again (gh-113157)"] [925 2 "// slot wrappers"] [962 2 "// method-wrapper (descrobject.c's wrapper_call, wrapper_repr, wrapper_richcompare, wrapper_hash, wrapper_members,"] [963 2 "// wrapper_getsets, wrapper_reduce; queue 290): a slot wrapper bound to its instance, no __func__ and no"] [964 2 "// delegation to the wrapper's attributes; not bound again as an attribute of a class (no tp_descr_get)"] [1004 2 "// classmethod_descriptor (descrobject.c's classmethod_get, classmethoddescr_call, method_repr, descr_reduce; queue"] [1005 2 "// 290): bound to the class it is asked through (a builtin_function_or_method whose __self__ is the class), called"] [1006 2 "// with the class first"] [1059 2 "// no __reduce__: PyClassMethodDescr_Type has no tp_methods (descrobject.c), so pickle refuses the descriptor"] [1060 2 "// itself (\"cannot pickle 'classmethod_descriptor' object\", test_pickle's test_c_methods), and dict.fromkeys, bound"] [1061 2 "// to its class, reduces as a method does"] [1063 2 "// classmethod, staticmethod (funcobject.c): a subclass's instance is an Instance around the Go value, so every"] [1064 2 "// slot unwraps; __init__ copies the wrapped callable's attributes (functools_wraps) into the dict"] [1090 19 "// a classmethod made by a program, not a built-in type's descriptor"] [1116 3 "// a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor: a builtin_function_or_method bound to the class (dict.fromkeys)"] [1174 3 "// descriptor_get_wrapped_attribute and its setter: the dict first, the callable's value kept there"] [1219 2 "// property"] [1234 2 "// property_init_impl (queue 304): a doc given, else the getter's (getter_doc); a subclass's instance gets it as its"] [1235 2 "// own __doc__ attribute (gh-41287), where a class's __slots__ without '__doc__' drops the getter's silently"] [1280 2 "// property_name: prop_name, else the getter's __name__ (nil when neither)"] [1290 2 "// the \"property %R of %R object has no getter\" family: the owner's __qualname__"] [1339 2 "// property_copy (queue 304): type(old)(get, set, del, doc), the doc None when the old one was the getter's and a"] [1340 2 "// getter is given, the name kept"] [1396 2 "// _PyObject_IsAbstract of each function: its __isabstractmethod__'s truth, an error propagated"] [1420 2 "// __slots__' members"] [1501 2 "// super"] [1548 5 "// a built-in type's method, or a method descriptor in a heap type's dict (methodDescrs: _ast's AST,"] [1549 5 "// queue 202c: super().__init__ in a node class's subclass)"] [1577 53 "// a subclass of super: its type called"] [1599 2 "// mappingproxy"] [1601 2 "// mappingproxy(mapping), over a dict (PY6a: enum's __members__); other mappings are the data model's"] [1609 3 "// an exact dict by its storage; a dict subclass (OrderedDict) as the mapping it is, so its repr and its"] [1610 3 "// comparison are its own (mappingproxy_new keeps the object; queue 278: inspect's Signature.parameters)"] [1614 3 "// mappingproxy_check_mapping: PyMapping_Check, not a list or a tuple"] [1627 2 "// a built-in type's own slots' wrappers (ownSlots, registry.go) are in its __dict__ too (PY5e, part 2b)"] [1635 14 "// a built-in type's attribute descriptors (type.__dict__['__annotations__']: annotationlib)"] [1667 2 "// mappingproxy_richcompare: the mapping's own comparison (queue 202: mappingproxy({}) == {} was False; test_re's"] [1668 2 "// test_getattr compares a pattern's groupindex with a dict)"] [1693 2 "// mappingproxy_or: the mappings beneath, a proxy's unwrapped on either side"] [1720 4 "// a built-in type's getsets and slot wrappers as its subscript has them (queue 290, 286's regression:"] [1721 4 "// enum's __set_name__ looks for int.__dict__.get('numerator') to redirect a shadowing member)"] [1760 41 "// type_set_name's PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize (queue 328)"] [1790 33 "// one object, as a static type's: pickle's memo shares it"] [1799 3 "// type_set_module: the class's __firstlineno__ goes with its old module (queue 278: inspect.getsource of"] [1800 3 "// _py_abc's ABCMeta, renamed into abc, raises OSError)"] [1835 21 "// inside the first mro()"] [1851 3 "// type_set_type_params' check_set_special_type_attr: no deletion, no immutable type (queue 328)"] [1889 2 "// type_get_text_signature: the signature in tp_doc, for the types that have one here (func_new's clinic doc)"] [1893 19 "// a C type's tp_doc signature (arbace/pyctypes, queue 270b)"] [1897 37 "// CPython's for a built-in type (queue 290), a heap type's from its __doc__"] [1905 33 "// type_mro: mro_implementation afresh, a metaclass's mro() builds on it"] [1918 3 "// queue 304: a built-in exception's built-in subclasses first (static_builtin_exceptions, readied at the"] [1919 3 "// interpreter's start: pydoc's \"Built-in subclasses\"); other built-in types keep only the classes made since"] [1920 3 "// (those the builtins module names: a module's exception, locale.Error, ssl.SSLError, comes with its module)"] [1949 3 "// recursive_issubclass's check_class"] [1974 1 "// checkSetSpecial is check_set_special_type_attr."] [2130 2 "// method_descriptor's members and getsets (descrobject.c